<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103955" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιλ-τός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>plucked, gathered</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάχανα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					2138.7
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>shredded</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. μοτός</span>
			<i>lint</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				11.125
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλλύχνιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					2.11
				</span></i>
			: also in neut. as Subst., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαμοτώσαντες ξηροῖς τιλτοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paul.Aeg.
					6.5
				</span></i>
			, cf. <u>Gloss.</u>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τ</span>. (with or without <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάριχος</span>) salt fish <i>stripped of its
				scales</i> before curing, <i><span class="en">
				Nicostr.Com.
				5.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.Com.
				193
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
